A8  m/Lambda from corpus m a ; two-loop asymptotic scaling
==============================================================================

[0] beta-function normalization, standard form
    beta(g) = dg/dln mu = -b0 g^3 - b1 g^5 + O(g^7)   [convention]
    b0 = 11N/(3 (4pi)^2) = 11N/(48 pi^2)
    b1 = 34N^2/(3 (4pi)^4) = 34N^2/(768 pi^4) = 34N^2/(3 (16 pi^2)^2)

    N |        b0 |        b1 |  b1/b0^2 | 102/121 | b0*48pi^2/11N | b1*768pi^4/34N^2
    2 | 0.046439 | 0.001818 | 0.842975 | 0.842975 | 1.000000000000 | 1.000000000000
    3 | 0.069658 | 0.004090 | 0.842975 | 0.842975 | 1.000000000000 | 1.000000000000

    cross-check vs textbook Nf=0 values (units of 1/(4pi)^2k):
    N=2: 11N/3 = 7.333333  vs b0*(4pi)^2 = 7.333333   ;  34N^2/3 = 45.333333  vs b1*(4pi)^4 = 45.333333
    N=3: 11N/3 = 11.000000  vs b0*(4pi)^2 = 11.000000   ;  34N^2/3 = 102.000000  vs b1*(4pi)^4 = 102.000000
    [T] b1/b0^2 = (34/3)(9/121) = 102/121 exactly, N-independent.

[1] a Lambda = exp(-1/(2b0g2)) (2 b0 g2)^(-b1/(2b0^2))
    g2 convention: beta_W = 2N/g2  =>  g2 = 2N/beta_W  (SU2: 4/b, SU3: 6/b)

    N=3, g2=1:  b0g2=0.069658  2b0g2=0.139317  1/(2b0g2)=7.17789  exp=7.632735e-04
    N=3, g2=1:  (2b0g2)^(-b1/2b0^2)=2.295050e+00   -> aLam=1.751751e-03
    truncation check, exact 2-loop closed form vs task formula (N=3,g2=1):
      exact=2.403243e-03  task=1.751751e-03  ratio=0.7289

