[8] scheme sensitivity: c = m/Lambda is NOT scheme independent
    a scheme change is a constant shift d(1/g2);  d ln(m/Lambda)/d(1/g2) = 1/(2 b0)
      N=2: 1/(2b0) = 10.7668  =>  d(1/g2)=0.5 moves m/Lambda by e^5.383 = 217.8x
      N=3: 1/(2b0) = 7.1779  =>  d(1/g2)=0.5 moves m/Lambda by e^3.589 = 36.2x
    to pull m/Lambda = 613 down to 1 needs d(1/g2) = ln(613)*2b0 = 0.894   (an ordinary O(1) matching constant)
    corpus has NO scheme matching (bare lattice g2 -> MS-bar): unchecked piece.

[9] internal a-ratio test (normalization-free)
    two-loop: a(6.30)/a(6.00) = aLam(6.30)/aLam(6.00) = 0.7130
    measured: m a(6.30)/m a(6.00)     = 0.8257   (same physical m assumed)
    => agreement within the ~18%% error: the beta-dependence of the formula is OK.
    physical anchor (probe-m/REPORT.md:150, Necco-Sommer r0/a=5.368,7.380,9.660):
      a^-1(6.0)=2.91 GeV  =>  m = 1.073*2.91 = 3.12 GeV ; m/Lambda_2loop with Lambda=5.1 MeV

[10] verdict
    (c) fires ON ITS FACE: m/Lambda = 3e2..7e2, i.e. 2.5-2.9 orders above 1.
    (b) DOES NOT fire: SU(3) 6.00 vs 6.30 -> 613 vs 709, diff -97 +- 137 = 0.71 sigma.
    (a) does NOT hold: the value is ~6e2, not O(0.1-3).
    normalization audit: b0,b1 = 11N/3, 34N^2/3 in 1/(4pi)^2k units, exact;
      b1/b0^2 = 102/121 exactly; b1/(2b0^2) = 0.4215 (a lost factor 2 here would
      move m/Lambda by (2b0g2)^{0.4215} = 0.44 -> checked); exact 2-loop closed form
      vs the task formula differs by -27.1% at g2=1. No factor-2/pi^2 slip can
      produce 6e2 from O(1).
    => c = m/Lambda is a scheme-conditional number at g2 ~ 1; not a pure number.

[11] SUMMARY
    (a) NOT supported: m/Lambda = 2.9e2..7.1e2, not O(0.1-3).
    (b) NOT fired: SU(3) two points agree (0.71 sigma); a-ratio 0.71 vs 0.83.
    (c) FIRED: m/Lambda > 1 by 2.5-2.9 orders -> normalization/interpretation check,
        done in [0],[1],[8]: arithmetic exact, the gap is the unsupplied scheme
        constant d(1/g2) ~ 0.9 (Lambda_2loop = 5.1 MeV vs physical ~2e2 MeV).
    => c = m/Lambda is NOT a pure number from these data; the corpus fixes its
       shape (beta-constant) but not its normalization.
